==English==

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/ɡɹɪl/}}
* {{audio|en-us-grill.ogg|Audio (US)}}
* {{rhymes|ɪl}}

===Etymology 1===
From {{etyl|enm}} {{term|grillen||to anger, provoke|lang=enm}}, from {{etyl|ang}} {{term|grillan|lang=ang}}, {{term|griellan||to annoy, vex, offend|lang=ang}}, from {{proto|Germanic|grellanan|to shout, make angry|lang=en}}, from {{proto|Indo-European|gʰer-|to rattle, make a noise, grumble|lang=en}}. Cognate with {{etyl|nl|-}} {{term|grillen||to shudder, shiver|lang=nl}}, {{etyl|nds|-}} {{term|vergrellen||to anger, provoke|lang=nds}}, {{etyl|de|-}} {{term|grollen||to rumble|lang=de}}.

====Alternative forms====
* {{l|en|girl}}

====Verb====
{{en-verb}}

# {{chiefly|Scotland|transitive}} to make [[angry]], [[provoke]]
# {{chiefly|Scotland|transitive}} to [[terrify]], make [[tremble]]
# {{chiefly|Scotland|intransitive}} to [[tremble]]; [[shiver]]
# {{context|Northern England|Scotland|intransitive}} to [[snarl]]; to [[snap]]

===Etymology 2===
From {{etyl|enm}} {{term|gril|lang=enm}}, {{term|grille||harsh, rough, severe|lang=enm}}, from {{etyl|ang|-}} *{{term||griell|lang=ang}}, from {{proto|Germanic|grellaz|angry|lang=en}}, from {{proto|Indo-European|gher-|to rattle, make a noise, grumble|lang=en}}. Cognate with {{etyl|de|-}} {{term|grell||harsh, angry|lang=de}}, {{etyl|da|-}} {{term|grel||shrill, glaring, dazzling|lang=da}}.

====Adjective====
{{en-adj|er|more}}

# [[harsh]], [[rough]], [[severe]]; [[cruel]]

====Noun====
{{en-noun|-|grills}}

# [[harm]]

===Etymology 3===
1655, from {{etyl|fr}} {{term|gril|lang=fr}}, from {{etyl|frm}}, from {{etyl|fro}} {{term|greïl|lang=fro}}, {{term|graïl||gridiron|lang=fro}}, from {{term|graïlle||grate, grating|lang=fro}}, from {{etyl|la}} {{term|craticula|crātīcula|gridiron|lang=la}}, diminutive of {{term|cratis|crātis|hurdle, wickerwork|lang=la}}, from {{proto|Indo-European|kor(ə)t-||krāt-|to weave, twist, wattle; wicker|lang=en}}. Related to {{l|en|griddle}}, {{l|en|hurdle}}.

====Alternative forms====
{{wikipedia}}
* [[grille]]

====Noun====
[[Image:Brazier.JPG|thumb|[[brazier|Brazier]] with '''grill''' and pot rest]]
{{en-noun}}

# A [[rack]]; a [[grid]] of [[wire]] or a sheet of material with a pattern of holes or slots, usually used to [[protect]] something while allowing the passage of [[air]] and [[liquid]]s. Typical uses: to allow air through a [[fan]] while preventing fingers or objects from passing; to allow people to talk to somebody, while preventing [[attack]].
# On a [[vehicle]], a [[slot]]ted cover as above, to protect and hide the [[radiator]], while admitting air to cool it.
# A device comprising a source of [[radiant]] [[heat]] and a means of holding food near it, to cook it; a [[barbecue]]; a [[griddle]].
#: ''I put some peppers and mushrooms on the '''grill''' to go with dinner.''
# {{colloquial}} A type of jewelry worn on the front teeth; by extension, the front teeth regarded collectively.

